guardrails/state/
# incident_memory/log.jsonl MUST be tracked — it is the cross-run "gets better"
# store; on an ephemeral runner an untracked log resets every cycle and the loop
# never learns. Ignore everything else under the dir, keep the log.
incident_memory/*
!incident_memory/log.jsonl
# Loop intermediates: raw agent output may carry log-sourced client data —
# never commit them. Patterns are RELATIVE to this file's dir, which is the dir
# the intermediates are written to (the repo root here, `.shl/`
# once vendored) — so a bare `*.json` is correct; a `.shl/`-
# prefixed pattern would look one level too deep and leak. `*.json` does not
# match the tracked `log.jsonl` (different extension).
*.json
# The OpenCode harness config is part of the install, not an intermediate: it
# carries the per-role permission blocks, and a target where it is missing has
# no restriction to select. Named explicitly so the blanket rule above keeps
# covering everything an agent writes.
!opencode.json
*.txt
*.diff
*.raw
__pycache__/
*.pyc